 200 /	D)	OFFSET - THE HANDLER CAN BE ASSEMBLED WITH NO OFFSET,  I.E.,  IT WOULD
 210 /	ADDRESS  THE  ABSOLUTE BEGINNING OF THE DEVICE (POSSIBLY BIASED BY AN  INTEGER
 220 /	MULTIPLE  OF  A  POWER  OF TWO BLOCKS INTO THE DEVICE) AND IS  MEANT  TO  HAVE
 230 /	INDEPENDENT DOMAIN OVER THE DEVICE.  THIS OPTION EXISTS FOR COMPATIBILITY WITH
 240 /	VARIOUS  OBSOLETE  MECHANISMS    WHICH    ARE   NOT  RECOMMENDED  FOR  CURRENT
 250 /	APPLICATIONS.
 260 /		THE PROPER MANAGEMENT OF DISK  DEVICES SUCH AS ARE USUALLY ATTACHED TO
 270 /	THE MDC8 REQUIRES THAT A DEVICE  MAINTAINENCE  AREA  BE RESERVED ON THE DEVICE
 280 /	FOR DEFECT MANAGEMENT, ETC.  THE MOST  COMPREHENSIVE  OF  THESE  IS THE MENU-8
 290 /	UTILITY SYSTEM WHICH ALLOWS SUBORDINATE SYSTEMS (SUCH AS  P?S/8)  TO BE LOADED
 300 /	INDIRECTLY.    PROPER  ASSEMBLY OF THE HANDLER FOR THIS  ENVIRONMENT  REQUIRES
 310 /	SETTING  THE OFFSET PARAMETER.  ALL LOGICAL BLOCKS ARE CONVERTED  TO  PHYSICAL
 320 /	BLOCKS BY ADDING A SMALL FIXED OFFSET (WHICH PLACES THE AFFECTED BLOCKS PAST A
 330 /	PROTECTED AREA WHERE THE MENU SYSTEM RESIDES).
