 350 /	E)	LOGUNIT - VARIOUS CONTROLLERS ALLOW LOGICAL UNIT VALUES TO BE ASSERTED
 360 /	FROM 0 THROUGH 7.  CERTAIN  CONTROLLERS  SUPPORT THE UNIT FIELD WITHIN THE I/O
 370 /	COMMAND,  BUT  RESTRICT USEFUL ACCESS TO LOGICAL  UNIT  0  ONLY.    (ON  THESE
 380 /	CONTROLLERS, OTHER LOGICAL UNIT VALUES RETURN "NOT READY",  "NOT  SELECTED" OR
 390 /	OTHER  SUCH ERRORS.)
 400 /		THE SUPPORTED OMTI CONTROLLERS ALLOW FOUR LOGICAL  UNITS (0-3), AS THE
 410 /	HIGH-ORDER LOGICAL UNIT BIT IS IGNORED.  CONTROLLER CONFIGURATION RULES EITHER
 420 /	RESTRICT  OR  RECOMMEND  (FOR COMPATIBILITY WITH MORE RESTRICTIVE CONTROLLERS)
 430 /	THE USE OF LOGICAL UNITS 0 AND 1 FOR WINCHESTER  DISK DRIVES.  OTHER UNITS MAY
 440 /	BE ASSIGNED TO OTHER DEVICES SUCH AS DISKETTE DRIVES, ETC.;   THE  CONTROLLERS
 450 /	GENERALLY  SUPPORT  ONLY  TWO  WINCHESTER  DRIVES MAXIMUM.  THE OMTI 20 SERIES
 460 /	CONTROLLERS RESTRICT THE USE OF LOGICAL UNITS 0 AND 1 TO WINCHESTERS ONLY, AND
 470 /	SPECIFY LOGICAL UNITS 2 AND 3 FOR DISKETTES.
 480 /		THE SUPPORTED  SYQUEST  555  REMOVABLE CARTRIDGE DRIVES (WITH PROPERLY
 490 /	FORMATTED SQ400 CARTRIDGES)  MUST  BE  ADDRESSED AS LOGICAL UNIT ZERO ONLY, AS
 500 /	THE SCSI CONTROLLER IS "IMBEDDED" IN THE HARDWARE OF THE PHYSICAL DRIVE, I.E.,
 510 /	IT IS AN INTEGRAL PART  OF  THE  DRIVE  ITSELF.    THE  SCSI  ID NUMBER MAY BE
 520 /	STRAPPED FOR ANY NON-CONFLICTING VALUE FROM  0  THROUGH  7  VIA JUMPERS ON THE
 530 /	OUTSIDE OF THE DRIVE (SEE SYQUEST DOCUMENTATION ELSEWHERE).
